      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "value": "\n<ol><li>Place the water used to extract the bran into [. . .]&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Take some of the ground lac with the sticks stripped away. Kn[ead it with some] of the</li>\n<li>clarified bran water. Grind it in a mortar, as a paste, very finely until it becomes like&nbsp;</li>\n<li>an ointment. Extract it with the bran water through a sieve of many holes until&nbsp;</li>\n<li>the lac sediment runs clear. Take the silk that has been treated with forty&nbsp;</li>\n<li>dirhams of splintered alum after it has soaked in the alum and water for a night and a day,&nbsp;</li>\n<li>and proceed to wash off the alum and wring it. Take half of the water containing&nbsp;</li>\n<li>the lac extract and place it in a copper vessel. Light a fire beneath it until it boils and splits,&nbsp;</li>\n<li>then skim off the foam. Lower the silk into it and reduce the fire. Do not cease turning it</li>\n<li>until it drinks up (the dye) and the water becomes clear. Take it out and rinse it in ample water, and do not. . . .</li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
      "motivation": [
